Barnaby sat by the door and listened.

Outside, the night was alive.

He could hear the whisper of leaves, the distant bark of a dog, the soft hum of insects in the grass. There was also something else: a faint, strange sound from the direction of the old oak tree. It was not a bird. It was not a squirrel. It was small and thin, like a voice calling for help.

